# Valgrind suppressions of the upstream noise the suites meet.
#
# The nginx of the suites is stopped with a signal, so a few allocations of the
# nginx core are reported as lost: the environment and the event module of the
# process, and the pools of the cycle and of the configuration.  Those are the
# records below:
#
#     ngx_set_environment()       24 bytes
#     ngx_event_process_init()    27,136 bytes
#     ngx_create_pool()           the cycle pool (ngx_init_cycle) and the
#                                 temporary pool of main()
#
# The frames under the ones written in each block depend on the process: the
# Test::Nginx templates run nginx with `master_process off`, the end to end
# suite runs a master with workers, and both were seen to end without the
# allocation of the other.  The blocks therefore match the top of the stack
# only, which is what identifies the record.
#
# The other two are the JIT of PCRE2 inside libmodsecurity: valgrind cannot
# follow code it did not generate itself, and every rule that reads a string
# reports an "Invalid read of size 16" or a conditional jump on a value it
# cannot track, both with their first frames in unknown code.  The
# suppressions valgrind proposes for those records are `obj:* obj:*`, which is
# what is written below; they hide every record whose first frames are in JIT
# or unknown code, not only the ones of libmodsecurity.  That is the price of
# running the ModSecurity cases under valgrind at all.
{
   ngx_waf_nginx_set_environment
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:ngx_alloc
   fun:ngx_set_environment
}
{
   ngx_waf_nginx_event_process_init
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:ngx_alloc
   fun:ngx_event_process_init
}
{
   ngx_waf_nginx_pool
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:posix_memalign
   fun:ngx_memalign
   fun:ngx_create_pool
}
{
   ngx_waf_libmodsecurity_pcre2_jit_read
   Memcheck:Addr16
   obj:*
   obj:*
}
{
   ngx_waf_libmodsecurity_pcre2_jit_cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   obj:*
   obj:*
}
